 "result_text": "I fixed it in `get_keys` in `sshtunnel.py`. I haven't run the tests or tried it against a real `~/.ssh`.\n\nThe cause was the `if host_pkey_directories is not None:` guard around the search loop. The constructor's default is `host_pkey_directories=None`, so the loop was skipped entirely and the `or [DEFAULT_SSH_DIRECTORY]` fallback never ran. I removed the guard. The loop now always runs and falls back to `DEFAULT_SSH_DIRECTORY` when no directories are given. The rest of the diff is just the loop dedented one level.\n\nOne behaviour change: `get_keys` now always looks for `id_rsa`, `id_dsa`, `id_ecdsa` and `id_ed25519` in the default directory. Previously, with the default arguments, it loaded none.",
